From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:27:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 172/342] Remote Control: a profile can send to one
 application, active or not

A profile follows the active application, as before, or sends to an
application chosen under "Send to" whether it is active or not (by
signature; "Start it if it isn't running" launches it on a press).

- A button can have a scripting command instead of its keystroke,
  written as for hey ("Bply of Window 0", "do TogglePlaying of Window 0",
  "set Seek of Window 0 to int64(5000000)", "with name=value and ...").
  ScriptCommand.cpp makes the message, as hey would; the add-on sends it
  to the target, or to the active application, without waiting. Held,
  a repeating button sends it again every 0.2 s, as keys repeat.
- Keystrokes of a profile with a target go straight to the target's
  first window (its focus view), instead of through the input stream.
- Templates "MediaPlayer, active or not" (its scripting suite; the volume
  keys to its window, since the suite only sets the volume) and
  one for a music player's commands, which set the target.
- A Test button presses the selected button as if from the remote, for
  profiles with a target (Control() code 'rcTB').

Profiles of version 1 load unchanged, following the active application.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
